#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1380.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199262} :activity/id #uuid "ee989efc-2e02-5faf-9663-d0e67a72db66" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050741 :topic/id #uuid "62cde46f-1bc8-533b-b62a-02ec7aac97f3" :topic/math-academy-id 4174} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199262 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199458 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we discuss a concept analogous to *center of mass* that applies to rotating bodies.\n\nRecall that the *center of mass* of a plane lamina is defined as the point $(\\bar{x},\\bar{y})$ in the coordinate plane where the entire mass of the lamina could be concentrated to produce the same *total moment* about the coordinate axes as the original laminar. \n\nAnalogously, the **radius of gyration** of a plane lamina is the distance $R$ from an axis of rotation $L$ that the entire mass $M$ of the lamina would need to be concentrated to produce the same *moment of inertia* as the original lamina. \n\n![](images/c9/c9999bf30a93a857db731488739f0a640edc7b91de907cd772b777489a011fb8.png)\n\nTo derive an explicit formula for the radius of gyration, recall that the moment of inertia of a particle $P$ of mass $m$ at a distance of $r$ from an axis of rotation equals\n\n$$\nmr^2.\n$$\n\nSo, for a particle of mass $M$ at a distance of $R$ from the axis of rotation $L,$ the moment of inertia about $L$ is given by\n\n$$\nMR^2.\n$$\n\nThe radius of gyration is defined as the distance $R$ that a particle of mass $M$ must be placed to give the same moment of inertia as the original lamina. Therefore, it is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\nI = MR^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about $L.$\n\nRearranging this equation, we find that the radius of gyration is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I}{M}}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "9694de04-ca38-5d55-a60f-6663ca34e7cf" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5074 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "76c2c5a5-4cc8-5b16-af7c-3ebae501b962" :step/math-academy-id 31767 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199368}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199344 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198417 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198059 :question/id #uuid "88848c23-66fe-5937-958c-28d73b593d99" :question/math-academy-id "e-12487"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049331}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198651} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198665} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235554} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281676} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281677} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281678} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435469} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435471} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435472} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435473} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435475} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444168} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444169}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Uniform Rectangular Laminar"} :step/id #uuid "b8d3d2ed-b979-53cc-a718-ce66bcb92672" :step/math-academy-id 44959 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199351}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199348 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198419 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198061 :question/id #uuid "fa3e8249-cb9f-50f6-a56f-6f311d101de6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12495"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "068d9714-bd1e-5036-a0c7-9be288831f52" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198663} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281681} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284396} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284397} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369943} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435474} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435477}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Radii of Gyration Using Polar Coordinates"} :step/id #uuid "4f7fed02-59a7-5116-a7d3-2d07448fbbfa" :step/math-academy-id 45033} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199351 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198421 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198063 :question/id #uuid "5245b67a-8beb-512d-b3c8-2d38db797703" :question/math-academy-id "e-12507"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198664} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198956} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281682} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281684} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281685} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281686} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326719} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369929} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369936} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370880} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435470} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435476}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar"} :step/id #uuid "b3e8808b-6d9a-533e-98f7-fae6b2f81961" :step/math-academy-id 45077 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199348}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199368 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199498 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll limit the axis of rotation to the $x$-axis, the $y$-axis, and the origin. We summarize the key results below:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ of a lamina about the $x$-axis is given by $R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$ where $I_x$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ of a lamina about the $y$-axis is given by $R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$ where $I_y$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ of a lamina about the origin is given by $R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$ where $I_0$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the origin." :tutorial/id #uuid "096487a4-3e7b-571a-94b9-ec4e84d689bd" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7823 :tutorial/title "A Summary of Key Results"} :step/id #uuid "b488dfc8-1a77-5eca-8218-1163bb51565d" :step/math-academy-id 45253 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199344}}] :activity/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198500}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444170} :activity/id #uuid "74cd288a-6d4e-5649-a0a3-fd1f66ef23c9" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050741 :topic/id #uuid "62cde46f-1bc8-533b-b62a-02ec7aac97f3" :topic/math-academy-id 4174} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444170 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281677 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8c3f43-d62e-5000-aa73-65488d3b0b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278693} {:answer/id #uuid "124a91eb-fdf5-5e37-9d33-f96d11c8d50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278758} {:answer/id #uuid "4cbbd3c2-db9a-55d6-97d8-e5b35b4b7f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279281} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8c9571-4624-5e8c-9ba9-3cb3cfed6da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279604} {:answer/id #uuid "d0235cb5-d166-53f6-8c2a-e428ad59a7f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280423} :answer-field/id #uuid "65cfd582-049a-5c5a-85d6-152e3b8591a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c52b9e07-a1a1-59e3-9b59-f3ce7c050afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-163578" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 3=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(1+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{10M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0e7b7881-d766-59e5-9ac2-17b4c071226f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444173}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444171 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e41b76a-dabb-5807-a6bb-5779e0a43c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278869} {:answer/id #uuid "59d4646c-a8cc-5cc4-8c20-a790ad2f4d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279413} {:answer/id #uuid "74959f37-361c-597f-97f4-79fda9c4ad64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279642} {:answer/id #uuid "ed79e371-e80a-5031-880e-b39448d43e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280675} {:answer/id #uuid "ee046b1f-ca21-54a9-88ec-7eeb4e214626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280677}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280675} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee676f82-5c11-53e9-9b1a-845255b4b041" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2496e287-b250-5877-a40c-af954399de62" :question/math-academy-id "q-163612" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\frac{1}{3}(1-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}[y]_{4}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(6-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "512ba0cc-ab8c-5fb2-8948-44914ec8fb98"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444172 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6535965a-826c-5401-b848-6255c9d1f28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279511} {:answer/id #uuid "7deac3bc-f281-52ad-8e6b-0601f71b4a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279719} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0ffd07-00a8-5c7d-b894-4de55fd2b939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279736} {:answer/id #uuid "e541680e-b07b-5177-9547-9e1ab1f2488d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280616} {:answer/id #uuid "eb846481-780f-5fe4-beca-6607afcf5a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280661}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280616} :answer-field/id #uuid "2495d518-218f-5140-a76c-b46562a88454" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3adab878-1dd3-5ac8-88b6-a5059624907c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163604" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the lines $y=x,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{4}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{5}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c02d457b-f21d-50f7-b09e-291abfa68047" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444174}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444173 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e358496-a583-59a6-b4e0-5fcf99d9cafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444157} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca9c9b8-05e4-5eb3-8122-ad72c6a359f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444158} {:answer/id #uuid "688f7ffe-b0fd-57c9-821e-0495e33a6fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444161} {:answer/id #uuid "9bbfff91-ca90-559f-ae5d-5fd328a1f1e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444163} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7abb37-0de9-58cb-8a76-9f11aa3adea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444165}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444163} :answer-field/id #uuid "02ef48a6-5de2-5aeb-b94d-50e269438d16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae31463b-0937-5dcb-a149-ee8482b71924" :question/math-academy-id "q-163579" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,2\\le y\\le 5\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 3=9.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}(\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}{\\int }_{2}^{5}21\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}[y]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}(5-2) \\\\  & =7M.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=7\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ce124292-03a7-514d-bbf3-a753805c4055" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444172}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444174 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020395fa-1c94-56f4-b0cf-6b542584a05e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444156} {:answer/id #uuid "4e9fa620-f201-58e2-aec9-4998cb5b396c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444159} {:answer/id #uuid "61c6c170-edd9-5422-8928-2559bb6d8200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{34}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444160} {:answer/id #uuid "7f05bbf6-f47e-5bba-ae07-b44dd179c296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{61}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444162} {:answer/id #uuid "aed2bb04-ea3b-5b55-b733-92f0f589ec24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444164}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444160} :answer-field/id #uuid "364a1bfa-3c03-5519-b8cb-713056748a8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a051470-22b3-5741-85c9-94876b2374fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-163606" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{64}{3}+4{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}21+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[21y+{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(63+27-21-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot 68 \\\\  & =\\frac{34M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{34}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{34}{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f1544047-bb8b-536b-b9d7-9b50cf101d4e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444171}}] :activity/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444155}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479155} :activity/id #uuid "315966ad-7330-535d-905a-0ad99188e4ab" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050741 :topic/id #uuid "62cde46f-1bc8-533b-b62a-02ec7aac97f3" :topic/math-academy-id 4174} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479150 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198651 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06aa15d2-30ee-5cc9-b5dd-ac324e05cd6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278654} {:answer/id #uuid "240de7aa-73fc-57f0-b478-71f4546ac6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278914} {:answer/id #uuid "578364b4-8440-58d4-999a-e71df76621b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279394} {:answer/id #uuid "8474f088-76e4-5da5-a9e4-54e62eda057e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279781} {:answer/id #uuid "8f9f0418-d641-5bc4-9599-2fdec0a94b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279869}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278654} :answer-field/id #uuid "2413e5c4-0b04-5b4f-a226-389f725261b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5e1eb104-83e6-5dc7-913b-3996107f92c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163011" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{4}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(4+9-(\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(13-\\frac{5}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{34}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{17}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "147cc4dc-7dc1-5126-916a-8cec1032d28e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479156}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479154 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "307a7ca4-01fa-5646-885b-a0e8867f3b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279016} {:answer/id #uuid "501aac95-5532-5856-a642-0d3b1d67f719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279322} {:answer/id #uuid "5327eac7-a93d-5b6d-af9d-e6bb83813164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279347} {:answer/id #uuid "9996b21a-d3a1-58ce-91cf-3cc1dfc91e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{21}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279948} {:answer/id #uuid "f72fd95a-5b27-5a58-83e0-471231a84783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280756}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279347} :answer-field/id #uuid "66c3c972-8140-526a-b8d9-d9d228cd316b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b31c8b99-cc6d-5598-a2c8-85f537ed1a0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163586" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5b8ddb36e814517af21d790374e1fb192141bd6ef0fd99e83a147c6ed5a62aea.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ and the coordinate axes, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3}{7}My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{7}Mr\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[-\\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-0+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}M\\cdot \\frac{31}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{31M}{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31M}{35}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{35}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5a28356f-4b44-5c8b-b9c7-4d02b2d94106"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479155 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f293b5e9-65d5-536c-b18d-a76dc4e7ea80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370882} {:answer/id #uuid "2e26a64f-d68e-5522-ac57-78a01cfc8093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370883} {:answer/id #uuid "de7b89dc-f977-5e1a-9b52-09259a14b526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370884} {:answer/id #uuid "6b112ea6-1937-5361-af39-bf68f7bc8dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370885} {:answer/id #uuid "696ba733-0b46-5f03-b9f3-48ae1fe194cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370886}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370886} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a96fbcd-7761-58d9-ae0a-eb2b94c9e2c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "defce080-8c65-59c1-a4eb-652286fe6d3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38819" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ the line $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=4My.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 4My\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =M{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{M}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6aa4a18d-6a7f-5ff6-bc60-411ff63cf5eb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479150}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479156 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28052605-ef85-5d61-b60d-35c652016958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278950} {:answer/id #uuid "30e535dc-d841-51b2-9346-6dd8f8151f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279019} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4a7fcf-e348-50c3-a268-aaa5fcf0d810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279712} {:answer/id #uuid "cd62681a-f336-57f7-9271-562c7877f73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280402} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cb850d-af3a-58fe-9a74-754886c3ca4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280620}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280620} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fb299df-44bd-5725-bf66-0524bf139842" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c58b6231-e237-5de8-8e27-d0ade4f5cce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-163576" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 3=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(8-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}[y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6eabb3c1-2352-5d3f-adb7-054c0b5fbb20" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479158}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479158 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d652bb7-2c2a-59df-a30e-8a26cac188ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278716} {:answer/id #uuid "78b8c404-1b74-574e-aaff-1cac4f74dbe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279668} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f6880e-c432-5d49-a344-3611d4439c6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280038} {:answer/id #uuid "bbd4a4e6-f500-5149-b052-7702a8b7faf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280245} {:answer/id #uuid "d680d34e-7009-583e-b502-5b6983be161b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280485}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278716} :answer-field/id #uuid "5840af3f-f19a-5638-befc-d037ec15bab6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "de217583-4705-57c2-81c7-b02676db7154" :question/math-academy-id "q-163582" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{7}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{7}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(7+9-\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{40}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{20M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{20}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{20}{3}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c726fa30-b86e-5568-af6e-dfea63974539" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479154}}] :activity/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478559}]}
